description.narrative:
The results obtained stem from the actions implemented through the objectives targeted by the program Sustainably contributing to meeting the freshwater needs of users and aquatic ecosystems. The indicator for this strategic objective is the "Level of satisfaction of users' water needs". Its reference situation was established through a study in 2018 at 62.1%. The level of satisfaction rose to 68.6% in 2022.

The important changes brought about through the support are:

- the application of the texts regulating the water sector through operationalization of water police services;

- the need to pay the parafiscal tax or the Financial Contribution in terms of Water is understood by all the actors intervening in the field of water;

- the adoption of good practices by water users through establishment of local water committees;

- the prevention of conflicts of use through awareness campaigns.

The evaluation of consideration of the perspectives of poverty, environment and climate, gender, human rights, conflict and security, in the implementation of the project revealed the following results:

- existence of a guide for integrating the Human Rights-Based Approach and gender equality in the establishment of Local Water Committees. Based on this guide, advocacy for consideration of gender dimension in the various IWRM bodies has made it possible to obtain 30% of women in the local water committees set up.

- protection of water resources takes into account the environment and climate.

- operationalization of Local Water Committees takes issues into account (gender, human rights, conflict).

- implementation of the IWRM national programme considers the poverty dimension.

Lessons learnt that may be useful for selection and management of future interventions :

In term of future intervention the project should:

- pursue total control of water around Water bodies, which is a priority for strengthening populations livelihoods;

- emphasize water reservoirs protection, in particular small dams which are subject to environmental threats or degradation and which compromise their sustainability;

- continue the search for agricultural sector performance: crop production is marked by a low level of use of inputs, equipment and innovative technologies;

- focus on strengthening the links between production and market.

Possible modifications that may be necessary in the project if it were to continue relate to the need for a support for PNGIRE actions towards emerging themes (Adaptation to climate change, conflict management, AFDH, etc.), knowledge of water resources, securing works and strengthening governance.
